// =============================================================================
// 07: "TEXAS FLOOD" — SLOW BURNING 12-BAR BLUES (Key of E — 48 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// Faithfully modeled after Stevie Ray Vaughan's legendary recording "Texas Flood"
// (1982). Crawling 48 CPM tempo in deep 12/8 triplet shuffle with the iconic
// Bar 2 Quick-Change to IV.
//
// 🎸 HOW TO JAM OVER "TEXAS FLOOD" (KEY OF E):
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// • E Minor Pentatonic + The Blue Note (Box 1, 12th Fret):
//    e |----------------------------12--15--|  (E, G)
//    B |--------------------12--15----------|  (B, D)
//    G |------------12--14-[15]-------------|  (G, A, [Bb = Blue Note!])
//    D |----12--14--------------------------|  (D, E)
//    A |----12--14-[15]---------------------|  (A, B, [Bb])
//    E |--12--15----------------------------|  (E, G)
//
// • Iconic Texas Flood Opening Lick:
//   Slow whole-step bend on the 14th fret of the G string (A bent up to B),
//   hold it with heavy vibrato, release slowly to 12th fret G, then resolve to 14th fret D!
//
// 🎼 12-BAR HARMONIC ROADMAP (WITH QUICK CHANGE):
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Bar 1  : [E7#9]             -> The SRV "Hendrix" tonic chord
// Bar 2  : [A9]               -> THE QUICK-CHANGE TO IV (The signature Texas Flood move!)
// Bar 3–4: [E7#9] [E7#9]      -> Back to home
// Bar 5–6: [A9]   [A9]        -> The IV Chord (Dig into crying bends!)
// Bar 7–8: [E7#9] [E7#9]      -> Home
// Bar 9  : [B9]               -> The V Chord (Peak emotional tension!)
// Bar 10 : [A9]               -> Resolving IV Chord
// Bar 11 : [E7#9]             -> Home
// Bar 12 : [B7#9]             -> The Turnaround (Dripping tension back to Bar 1)
//
// 🎛️ CONTROLS (<leader> = Space in Neovim):
//   <leader>ml : :StrudelLaunch (Connect to Strudel engine)
//   <leader>mp : :StrudelToggle (Play / Pause backing track)
//   <leader>mu : :StrudelUpdate (APPLY CHANGES LIVE — Press after uncommenting!)
//   gcc        : Toggle comment on a line (1 tap to introduce/mute a layer)
// =============================================================================


// =============================================================================
// 🌧️ TRACK 1: "TEXAS FLOOD" (Ultra-Slow 12/8 Triplet Shuffle — 48 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// LIVE-BUILDING FLOW:
//   Starts with ONLY Layer 1 active (dripping E7#9 chords with deep hall reverb).
//   Play your slow guitar intro over the chords, then introduce layers one-by-one:
//   Line 53: Swung Bass | Line 56: Shuffle Hat | Line 59: Wet Snare | Line 62: Kick

stack(
  // [Step 1 - ACTIVE AT START] Dripping Slow Blues Chords (with Quick-Change to IV)
  note("<[e3,gs3,d4,g4] [a2,g3,cs4,fs4] [e3,gs3,d4,g4]!2 [a2,g3,cs4,fs4]!2 [e3,gs3,d4,g4]!2 [b2,a3,ds4,g4] [a2,g3,cs4,fs4] [e3,gs3,d4,g4] [b2,a3,ds4,g4]>")
    .s("triangle")
    .lpf(1100)
    .room(0.88)
    .decay(1.2)
    .gain(0.42),

  // [Step 2 - BASS] Tommy Shannon's Swung Triplet Blues Bass (Press gcc here)
  // note("<[e1 ~ e1 gs1 ~ gs1 b1 ~ b1 cs2 ~ cs2] [a1 ~ a1 cs2 ~ cs2 e2 ~ e2 fs2 ~ fs2] [e1 ~ e1 gs1 ~ gs1 b1 ~ b1 cs2 ~ cs2]!2 [a1 ~ a1 cs2 ~ cs2 e2 ~ e2 fs2 ~ fs2]!2 [e1 ~ e1 gs1 ~ gs1 b1 ~ b1 cs2 ~ cs2]!2 [b1 ~ b1 ds2 ~ ds2 fs2 ~ fs2 gs2 ~ gs2] [a1 ~ a1 cs2 ~ cs2 e2 ~ e2 fs2 ~ fs2] [e1 ~ e1 gs1 ~ gs1 b1 ~ b1 cs2 ~ cs2] [b1 ~ b1 ds2 ~ ds2 fs2 ~ fs2 gs2 ~ gs2]>").s("triangle").lpf(320).decay(0.6).gain(0.68),

  // [Step 3 - SHUFFLE] True 12/8 Texas Triplet Shuffle Cymbal: 1 - a, 2 - a, 3 - a, 4 - a (Press gcc here)
  // s("[hh ~ hh]!4").gain(0.3),

  // [Step 4 - SNARE] Chris Layton's heavy backbeat snare on 3 with wet hall reverb (Press gcc here)
  // s("~ ~ sd ~").room(0.85).gain(0.7),

  // [Step 5 - KICK] Single deep heartbeat pulse on beat 1 (Press gcc here to anchor!)
  // s("bd ~ ~ ~").lpf(280).gain(0.55),

  // [Step 6 - ORGAN] Hammond B3 Leslie swell (Press gcc here for extra blues soul!)
  // note("<[e3,b3,d4,gs4] [a2,g3,cs4,e4] [e3,b3,d4,gs4]!2 [a2,g3,cs4,e4]!2 [e3,b3,d4,gs4]!2 [b2,a3,ds4,fs4] [a2,g3,cs4,e4] [e3,b3,d4,gs4] [b2,a3,ds4,fs4]>").s("sine").lpf(sine.range(800, 1600).slow(8)).room(0.9).gain(0.3),
).cpm(48)


